From d79d8c91b019df634661988a5ff46216304da450 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 04:43:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 227/638] chrome: add the portable Aura browser frame for AROS
 [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-phase-4-browser-link

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: The upstream Chrome executable linked browser UI call sites on AROS but omitted the portable desktop Views sources and had no platform implementations for top-level native widgets, browser desktop hosts, status tray creation, or proxy settings.

FIX_REASON: Reuse Chromium's DesktopNativeWidgetAura and DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform contracts over the native AROS Ozone backend, enable the existing portable desktop UI source set, and fail visibly for the two OS integrations AROS does not yet provide.

SCOPE: chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn plus four AROS Views/WebUI platform implementations.

VALIDATION: GN regenerated out/aros-chrome; obj/chrome/browser/ui/libui.a completed all 766 build edges; git diff --cached --check passes.

RISK: medium; the frame path is new but delegates window creation to already validated Aura/Ozone machinery. Status tray and proxy settings are explicit nonfatal capability boundaries.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap;
